  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Positioning Dutch aquaculture sector in Indonesia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Asian Development Bank (ADB) has allocated a US$ 200 million loan to develop the aquaculture sector in Indonesia. The primary objective of this project is to provide a concise value proposition of Dutch aquaculture solutions to the Indonesian Implementing Agency and ADB Regional Mission.A white paper will be written. This paper will serve as a summary of the key benefits and advantages of these solutions. The presentation of this white paper will help improve the position of Dutch companies operating in the aquaculture sector. This will increase the chances of successfully obtaining ADB contracts.By having a better-positioned Dutch Consortium, the likelihood of Dutch companies and knowledge institutions becoming successful in the aquaculture sector in Indonesia will increase. Indonesia will benefit from the Netherlands&apos; world-class knowledge and skills in this respective sector.</narrative>
  </description>
